
8. File Handling: To perform file operations in Java. 

a) Create and write data into a file using FileWriter. 
b) Read data using FileReader and BufferedReader.
c) Append data to existing file. 
d) Count number of words/lines in a file.

a) Create and write data into a file using FileWriter. 

Aim:
To write a simple Java program to create a file and write data into it using the FileWriter class.

Program :- 

import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;

public class FileWriterExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        try {
            // Create and write to the file
            FileWriter writer = new FileWriter("sample.txt");
            writer.write("Welcome to Java File Handling.");
            writer.close();

            System.out.println("Data written to file successfully.");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("An error occurred.");
        }
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

Data written to file successfully.


b) Read data using FileReader and BufferedReader.

Aim
To write a simple Java program to read data from a file using FileReader and BufferedReader.

Program :- 

import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.IOException;
public class FileReaderExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            FileReader fr = new FileReader("sample.txt");
            BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(fr);

            String line;

            System.out.println("File Contents:");

            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println(line);
            }
            br.close();
            fr.close();

        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("File not found.");
        }
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

File Contents:
Welcome to Java File Handling.

c) Append data to existing file. 

Aim
To write a simple Java program to append data to an existing file using the FileWriter class.

Program :-

import java.io.FileWriter;
import java.io.IOException;

public class AppendFileExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        try {
            // Append data to the existing file
            FileWriter writer = new FileWriter("sample.txt", true);

            writer.write("\nThis is appended text.");
            writer.close();

            System.out.println("Data appended successfully.");

        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("An error occurred.");
        }
    }
}

OUTPUT :- 

Data appended successfully.
Welcome to Java File Handling.
This is appended text.


d) Count number of words/lines in a file.

Aim
To write a Java program to count the number of words and lines in a text file.

PROGRAM :- 

import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;

class CountWordsLines
{
    public static void main(String args[]) throws Exception
    {
        File file = new File("sample.txt");
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(file);

        int lines = 0;
        int words = 0;

        while (sc.hasNextLine())
        {
            String line = sc.nextLine();
            lines++;

            String w[] = line.split(" ");
            words = words + w.length;
        }
        sc.close();
        System.out.println("Number of Lines = " + lines);
        System.out.println("Number of Words = " + words);
    }
}

